<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Keep this a superset of the generated library's TargetFrameworks
         (see _generateCSharpProjectFile in src/struct_frame/generate.py).
         run_tests.py picks one TFM from the installed .NET SDK version unless
         SF_DOTNET_TFM overrides it, and building a TFM this project does not
         declare fails with NETSDK1047. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <StartupObject>TestRunner</StartupObject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Seeing "CS0246: The type or namespace name 'StructFrame' could not be found
       (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)"

       Then the generated library is missing, not this reference. Regenerate it:

           python test_all.py

       (or run tests/run_tests.py with the only-generate flag to skip the tests).

       Do NOT delete the ItemGroup below to make that error go away. It resolves
       ..\generated\csharp\StructFrame.csproj, which is generated and gitignored,
       and is the ONLY source of the StructFrame namespace: there is no NuGet
       package and no shared source glob. Removing it does not fix the missing
       library, it just turns one problem into hundreds of CS0246 errors across
       every test file, plus "Negative Tests: C# - negative-test runner missing".
       This ItemGroup has been deleted and restored repeatedly for that reason.

       How the library usually goes missing: a `dotnet build` run by hand leaves
       the .NET build server holding directory handles under tests/generated/csharp.
       The next clean() then deletes that folder's contents but cannot remove the
       folder itself (WinError 32), so the run aborts with the library already gone.
       run_tests.py now shuts the build server down before cleaning, retries the
       delete, and fails loudly rather than continuing on a half deleted tree. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\generated\csharp\StructFrame.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
